GTK4 mp3x maintainer notes
==========================

Scope and build
---------------

`mp3x` is the GTK4 frame-analyzer frontend. It is optional and requires
GTK 4.10 or newer, libmpg123 1.26 or newer with decoder support enabled,
and analyzer hooks:

    autoreconf -fi
    ./configure --enable-mp3x
    make
    ./frontend/mp3x [LAME options] [input.wav|input.aiff|input.mp3|-]

The legacy GTK 1.2 sources remain in release archives through `EXTRA_DIST`,
but are not compiled. `mp3x_ui.c`, `mp3x_plot.c`, `mp3x_core.c`, and
`mp3x_session.c` are the only implementation units for the GTK4 executable.

Architecture and lifetime
-------------------------

`Mp3xDriver` is process/UI lifetime state. It borrows the application and
window, owns the current session, menu model, CSS provider, view preferences,
async-request identity slots, session-generation counter, and the cumulative
analysis-failure exit latch.

`Mp3xSession` is one open input. It owns its `lame_t`, path/display-name, and
transport state. Closing removes its idle source first, shuts down the core
decoder, calls `close_infile()`, closes the LAME handle, and frees its strings.
Opening another file restores the captured startup frontend-global baseline,
so CLI raw/format options cannot leak into a later GUI-selected file.

Each file-dialog request owns a strong driver reference, dialog, cancellable,
and one matching `g_application_hold()`. Its completion route releases all four
on completion. Each idle source owns a strong driver reference plus the captured
session pointer/generation and frees them in its destroy notify. A stale async
callback must match both the driver state epoch and session generation before
using session state.

The GUI prevalidates a selected `GFile` before retiring the
current session. A successful `Mp3xPrevalidateResult` owns its three strings
until they are either cleared or stolen by the replacement session.

Transport and EOF
-----------------

Input exhaustion and display completion are different states. For PCM input,
the first `mp3x_core_step()` returning zero has already shifted the ring, called
`lame_encode_flush()` once, fed its complete output to HIP, and decoded at most
one queued frame. The session then performs exactly `READ_AHEAD - 1`
`mp3x_core_drain_step()` shifts. Their first calls collect any remaining HIP
output already queued by the encoder flush; once HIP needs more data they shift
invalid sentinels. Drain steps do no input, encoding, or statistics work.
Completion is set only when the final real frame reaches the display position.
Play, repeated Step, and Last/Advance therefore reach the same final frame with
its correctly mapped Re-synthesis companion.

`frames_done` counts real analyzed frames only. Every real plotting slot stores
`totbits == sum(mainbits[gr][ch])`. A negative core result stops the session and
latches process exit status 1; a later successful open does not erase it.

CLI behavior
------------

Initial command-line parsing happens before `GtkApplication` is created.
The existing parser's informational result (`-2`) prints help, version,
license, usage, long-help, or genre-list output once and exits 0 without a
window. Parser/open failures exit nonzero. A successfully opened CLI session is
installed when GTK activates. Subsequent GUI Opens use documented clean
defaults rather than replaying the initial argv.

Plotting and export
-------------------

On-screen titles use a Pango layout created from the drawing widget, inheriting
its font map, font description, direction, DPI, and desktop text scaling.
Offscreen PNGs use a deterministic PangoCairo `Sans 11` layout. A measured title
band is excluded from every graph's data mapping. Drawing areas publish
accessible labels.

Every PNG writer checks the image surface, Cairo context, and
`cairo_surface_write_to_png()` status. Interactive Save/Export reports the
returned error instead of claiming success.

Test-only instrumentation
-------------------------

Production builds contain no environment-variable automation behavior. To
compile the opt-in validation hooks:

    ./configure --enable-mp3x CPPFLAGS=-DMP3X_ENABLE_TEST_HOOKS
    make

Only that build recognizes:

* `MP3X_START_PAUSED` - analyze one transition, then wait.
* `MP3X_STEP_TO_END` - exercise repeated paused Step transitions to completion.
* `MP3X_ADVANCE_TO_END` - exercise Last/Advance-to-end.
* `MP3X_QUIT_WHEN_DONE` - quit after completion or injected failure.
* `MP3X_FAIL_AFTER=N` - inject an analyzer failure after N real frames.
* `MP3X_STATE_REPORT=path` - write final frame/drain/totbits invariants plus
  the final Re-synthesis companion offset and decoded PCM peak.
* `MP3X_SHOT`, `MP3X_SHOT_RESYNTH`, `MP3X_SHOT_MDCT`,
  `MP3X_SHOT_MDCT1`, `MP3X_SHOT_PSY`, `MP3X_SHOT_PSY1`,
  `MP3X_SHOT_SFB`, `MP3X_SHOT_SFB1`, `MP3X_SHOT_COMPOSITE` - save all
  nine final plot artifacts.
* `MP3X_CHANNEL`, `MP3X_MS`, `MP3X_DIFF`, `MP3X_SOURCE`,
  `MP3X_NOSFBLINES`, `MP3X_KBFLAG` - override display choices.

Suggested regression matrix
---------------------------

1. Fresh normal and instrumented builds; changed files warning-clean.
2. Timeout-bound every informational CLI route and one invalid option.
3. WAV, AIFF, and MP3 inputs shorter than and longer than `READ_AHEAD`.
4. Play, repeated Step, and Last/Advance to the same final displayed frame.
5. Verify every reported `totbits` against the four `mainbits` fields, and
   require a Re-synthesis companion for every displayed final frame (a silent
   fixture may legitimately report a zero decoded PCM peak).
6. Empty, directory, missing, unreadable, and nonregular selections.
7. Repeated Open/Recent/Close/cancel/save cycles under the platform leak tool.
8. All nine PNG save routes, including an unwritable destination.
9. Channel/source/difference/SFB/subblock/spectrum controls, statistics,
   keyboard transport, fullscreen, and file replacement.
10. Confirm a normal binary contains none of the `MP3X_*` hook strings.
